message.content:
Roof racks for motor vehicles are generally classified as parts and accessories of motor vehicles in heading 8708 (HTSUS 8708.29.5160 or 8708.99). CBP rulings on roof racks, such as cross bars and luggage carriers, have placed them in 8708.99.8180, "Other parts and accessories: other: other: other." Others have placed them in 8708.29 (body parts). A permanently mounted roof rack is typically an accessory, so it falls under 8708.99.

The remaining question is whether the 8708.99 subheading is right. Roof racks are not stampings of 8708.29. The 8708.99 breakdown is 8708.99.03 (Drive axles... no), 8708.99.27 (Steering...), 8708.99.31 (Parts of power-steering), 8708.99.4 (Other: Frames), 8708.99.49, 8708.99.55 (Other: Of iron or steel...), 8708.99.68 (Other: Of aluminum? no), 8708.99.81 (Other: other), and 8708.99.8180 (Other). Roof racks are therefore commonly assigned 8708.99.8180 for being "other."

{"hts_code": "8708.99.8180", "reason": "A vehicle-specific roof rack kit permanently mounted on a motor vehicle is a motor vehicle accessory of heading 8708, falling in the residual 'other parts and accessories: other' provision."}
